From eb1803f4c095815056fd7a645b1790c46b7b5a79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:50:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 139/139] arm64: dts: qcom: describe SM8150 PRNG safely

Qualcomm downstream SM8150 device trees describe the execution-environment
PRNG block at 0x793000 behind GCC_PRNG_AHB_CLK. Add the corresponding
upstream binding-compatible node so Linux owns the block and its clock
state.

Keep the upstream trust boundary intact: qcom,prng-ee remains
ineligible for HWRNG registration, while the architectural SMCCC provider
registers only when higher firmware advertises a true TRNG. Pin both
decisions in the final Nabu config and document static and device HIL
gates.

Signed-off-by: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi |  7 +++++
 senemos/configs/nabu-rng.config      | 10 ++++++
 senemos/hil/nabu-rng-hil.md          | 47 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 64 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 senemos/configs/nabu-rng.config
 create mode 100644 senemos/hil/nabu-rng-hil.md

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
index 310d299ee..e81f0e4db 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
@@ -997,6 +997,13 @@ gpu_speed_bin: gpu-speed-bin@133 {
 			};
 		};
 
+		rng: rng@793000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,prng-ee";
+			reg = <0 0x00793000 0 0x1000>;
+			clocks = <&gcc GCC_PRNG_AHB_CLK>;
+			clock-names = "core";
+		};
+
 		qupv3_id_0: geniqup@8c0000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,geni-se-qup";
 			reg = <0x0 0x008c0000 0x0 0x6000>;
diff --git a/senemos/configs/nabu-rng.config b/senemos/configs/nabu-rng.config
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..0aac92cc9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/senemos/configs/nabu-rng.config
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Nabu entropy-source support.
+#
+# SM8150 exposes the legacy PRNG execution-environment block. Keep the
+# upstream qcom-rng classification: qcom,prng-ee is not a NIST SP800-90B TRNG
+# and must not be credited as trusted kernel entropy. Also build the standard
+# SMCCC TRNG provider; it registers only when higher firmware advertises the
+# architectural TRNG interface.
+CONFIG_HW_RANDOM=y
+CONFIG_HW_RANDOM_ARM_SMCCC_TRNG=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_QCOM_RNG=y
diff --git a/senemos/hil/nabu-rng-hil.md b/senemos/hil/nabu-rng-hil.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..01cfd4b14
--- /dev/null
+++ b/senemos/hil/nabu-rng-hil.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Nabu RNG validation
+
+## Trust boundary
+
+SM8150 vendor sources describe the execution-environment PRNG at `0x793000`
+with `GCC_PRNG_AHB_CLK`. Linux represents this block as `qcom,prng-ee`.
+The upstream qcom-rng driver deliberately does not register PRNG or PRNG-EE
+blocks as `hwrng`; only hardware described as `qcom,trng` is treated as a true
+entropy source. Do not relabel this node as `qcom,trng` and do not change the
+driver's `hwrng_support` flag without silicon documentation and independent
+entropy validation.
+
+The arm64 SMCCC TRNG driver is built in as a second, fail-closed path. It
+registers `smccc_trng` only when the higher exception-level firmware advertises
+the architectural TRNG interface. EFI random-seed input, a described PRNG
+block and a registered HWRNG are separate claims and must be reported
+separately.
+
+## Static gates
+
+1. Require `CONFIG_HW_RANDOM=y`, `CONFIG_HW_RANDOM_ARM_SMCCC_TRNG=y` and
+   `CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_QCOM_RNG=y` in the final merged configuration.
+2. Run `dtbs_check` for the Nabu Iris/camera DTB and require the PRNG node to
+   match `Documentation/devicetree/bindings/crypto/qcom,prng.yaml`.
+3. Decompile the built DTB and verify the compatible, register range and GCC
+   clock phandle instead of accepting source text alone.
+4. Keep `qcom_prng_ee_match_data.hwrng_support` false.
+
+## Device gates
+
+After a clean boot, record the kernel release, DTB and UKI hashes, then collect:
+
+```text
+dmesg -T | grep -Ei 'random|rng|smccc'
+cat /sys/class/misc/hw_random/rng_available
+cat /sys/class/misc/hw_random/rng_current
+cat /proc/sys/kernel/random/entropy_avail
+```
+
+If `smccc_trng` is available, read at least 16 MiB from `/dev/hwrng`, reject
+I/O errors, short reads and an all-zero stream, and repeat after ten suspend /
+resume cycles. Run repetition-count and adaptive-proportion health tests before
+crediting the provider in production. Generic statistical suites can detect
+obvious failures but cannot certify entropy.
+
+If no provider registers, report the result as `firmware TRNG unavailable`.
+Do not work around it by forcing the SM8150 PRNG-EE node into the HWRNG class.
